Unlock LiteLLM features whose MIT-licensed implementations sit behind
premium_user license gates (code outside enterprise/; the image has no
license). Each feature already runs without enterprise code.

- Premium key/team/org metadata (tags, guardrails, policies, logging, prompts,
  allowed_passthrough_routes, secret_manager_settings,
  disable_global_guardrails): premium_user_check refuses nothing, at save
  time and at request time. The same check also gates the SCIM v2 router and
  the GCS Pub/Sub and Azure Storage loggers. team_member_key_duration is
  accepted but has no MIT implementation, so it has no effect.
  Its legacy _premium_user_check alias follows it; require_enterprise_license
  still gates unreviewed features such as hosted admin MCP.
- Per-model budgets (model_max_budget) on keys and teams; users already
  accept them.
- Key regeneration, including the scheduled rotation that calls it.
- Team admins through /team/member_add and /team/member_update.
- Audit log writes. Storing them stays opt-in through
  litellm_settings.store_audit_logs; the /audit read API is enterprise code.
- The Admin UI's region outage alert TTL setting (/alerting/settings) is no
  longer marked premium; the alerts already run without a license.

Checks: tests/verify_premium_features.py

